From: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: qualcomm: drop Wave 7 bring-up logging

The direct QCA8081/MPPE SGMII path is now stable with the UNIPHY
external-PHY reference clock modeled through CCF. Remove the remaining
bring-up-only register snapshot from the functional post-MAC reset fix.

Keep all PCS sequencing, delays and adapter resets unchanged.

Signed-off-by: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
@@ -775,7 +775,6 @@ int ipq_pcs_link_up_post_mac(struct phylink_pcs *pcs)
 {
 	struct ipq_pcs_mii *qpcs_mii = phylink_pcs_to_qpcs_mii(pcs);
 	struct ipq_pcs *qpcs = qpcs_mii->qpcs;
-	unsigned int ctrl, sts;
 	int ret;
 
 	if (!qpcs->mppe || qpcs->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII)
@@ -797,11 +796,6 @@ int ipq_pcs_link_up_post_mac(struct phylink_pcs *pcs)
 		return ret;
 
 	fsleep(10000);
-	if (!regmap_read(qpcs->regmap, PCS_MII_CTRL(qpcs_mii->index), &ctrl) &&
-	    !regmap_read(qpcs->regmap, PCS_MII_STS(qpcs_mii->index), &sts))
-		dev_info(qpcs->dev,
-			 "MPPE SGMII post-MAC reset: ctrl=%#x sts=%#x\n",
-			 ctrl, sts);
 
 	return 0;
 }
